  screenshot: {fileID: 0}
  description: '{player} just moved into a first apartment with an empty wallet
    and a laptop that barely works. Mom says to have fun, but the bills are already
    coming in.'
  learningGoals:
  - What a monthly budget is
  - Needs vs. wants
  - Tracking where your money goes
  unlockedByDefault: 1
  summary:
  - choiceKey: insurance
    sentences:
    - value: bought
      sentence: You <b>bought the home insurance</b>.
      otherOption: If you hadn't, you'd have kept SEK 1,500 this month.
    - value: none
      sentence: You <b>didn't buy the home insurance</b>.
      otherOption: Buying it would have cost SEK 1,500 this month.
    sentenceIfNotChosen: 
    otherOptionIfNotChosen: 
  - choiceKey: vlog_recording
    sentences:
    - value: true
      sentence: You <b>turned on the vlog camera</b>.
      otherOption: 
    sentenceIfNotChosen: You <b>didn't turn on the vlog camera</b>.
    otherOptionIfNotChosen: 
  - choiceKey: insurance
    sentences:
    - value: bought
      sentence: Insurance <b>paid for your broken laptop</b>.
      otherOption: Without insurance, the repair would have cost you SEK 12,000.
    - value: none
      sentence: You <b>paid SEK {laptop_cost} for the broken laptop yourself</b>.
      otherOption: With insurance, the repair would have been covered.
